00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.420
which I like to sort of talk
about in all of my classes,

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:18.580
we are at very interesting times,
at crossroads, really.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.390
And that requires us to take
all of these frameworks that

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.900
you're learning in finance or
other classes and push them, really,

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.280
in directions that we haven't
sort of really tested.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:34.250
So, business, government policy, society,
they're all interacting in ways,

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.940
and making changes at a pace,
that we haven't seen before.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:43.527
There's disruption, innovation, but they
are disrupted, and a large number of them.

00:04:43.527 --> 00:04:47.214
There is growth, but
there is also polarization.

00:04:47.214 --> 00:04:50.659
And then there's government, which is
trying to balance all of these different

00:04:50.659 --> 00:04:54.000
constituents, sometimes successfully,
sometimes not so much.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.050
And, in this ecosystem,
in this environment, the question for

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.456
you all, like the committee posed,
they stole my thunder,

00:05:00.456 --> 00:05:04.120
is how are you going to define success.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.060
What's success for you?

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.000
It could be about innovating.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.790
It could be about
generating free cashflows,

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.830
making money, a lot of jobs, growth.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.270
But I'm hoping that you'll be more
fearless coming out of GSB, and

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.840
I'm going to push this
a little bit further.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:22.660
And when you do that, free cash flows
are not going to be free anymore.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.030
It'll require you to challenge yourselves,
and

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:31.010
redefine what you mean by success,
pretty regularly, really.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:36.370
And when you do, I'm hoping, that when you
go out from GSB, you will come back and

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.170
give us inputs and

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:43.730
feedback, like you have while you
were here, so that you challenge us.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.625
Because that's the only way we build
knowledge stock on which the next

00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:50.160
generations can really build on.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.650
And, you know, I like to call it
standing on the shoulders of giants,

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:58.170
which is all of you and us, where next
generations can stand and look far.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:02.280
But I was at a Midwest GST where I was
told, No, no no, that is old school.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.410
The new thing is you're standing
on the shoulders of dinosaurs.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.870
Because then you can see even further.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:11.393
So whatever, you guys need to go out and
then come back, and

00:06:11.393 --> 00:06:15.280
let us know what are we doing right and
what are we not doing wrong.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:21.250
But the bottom is that the problems
are complex and the solutions are unknown.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:26.010
But my hope is that all of you
who have taken my classes, and

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.620
